      "username": "fjur",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/{size}/4849_2.png",
      "created_at": "2022-10-01T22:54:25.218Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Godai\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"29657\" data-full=\"true\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/godai/48/1920_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Godai:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I am once again asking for the polls on this site to use contrasting colors, not similar colors</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Well, I’m afraid that I can’t do anything about that, unfortunately.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"TakeWalker\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"29657\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/48/5677_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TakeWalker:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>And like, a smaller pie chart. c.c I can’t scroll it right!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"MindWanderer\" data-post=\"4\" data-topic=\"29657\" data-full=\"true\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/48/4816_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MindWanderer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yeah, all I can see is a quarter of the graph, and it’s all blue with a sliver of black.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That is <em>very</em> unusual. Why would it do that? A bug, perhaps.</p>\n<p>I can see the whole graph on my smartphone, but not on a tablet. I haven’t tried to view it on a desktop. Curiouser and curiouser . . .</p>\n<p>Anyways, I don’t think that I can fix the chart, but I can post the results thus far for everyone to see:<br>\n<strong>6 votes — Analytical</strong><br>\n<strong>2 votes each — Inquisitive &amp; Lone Wolf</strong><br>\n<strong>1 vote each — Arrogant, Mischievous, Stoic, &amp; Nurturing</strong></p>\n<p>I suppose that I shouldn’t be surprised that the three top Personalities are all stereotypically geeky. : )</p>\n<p>I will admit that I am one of the six analytics. It was between either that or Inquisitive, but I believe that I also possess shades of several of the other Personalities.</p>",
